
is sliding window and two pointers the same?

two pointers — two indices moving through data to solve a problem, can move toward each other or in the same direction. broader concept.

sliding window — a specific type of two pointers where the pointers define a window that slides in one direction, typically used for substring/subarray problems.

so all sliding windows use two pointers, but not all two pointer problems are sliding windows.


