array.includes() scans the entire array every time it's called — that's O(n) per check, inside a loop that runs n times, giving O(n²) total.
set.has() is O(1) — it looks up the value instantly using hashing. Since the Set is already built from the repeat loop, you just reuse it instead of scanning the array again.


